Station T-25, located in survey area T, consists of four interpreted resistivity layers. The sequence begins with a top layer of 92.8 ohm-m, followed by a decreasing trend through the second layer (69.4 ohm-m) and the third layer (27.8 ohm-m). The resistivity increases again in the fourth layer to 47.2 ohm-m. 

Applying the vertical electrical sounding (VES) notation rules, the first three layers (92.8 > 69.4 > 27.8) characterize a Q-type sequence, while the second group of three layers (69.4 > 27.8 < 47.2) characterizes an H-type sequence. This results in a QH curve type, which is consistent with the survey classification currently on file.

